WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.770
Leah: Physical bullying, is the
most obvious form of bullying and

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.840
physical bullies, usually tend
to be bigger, stronger, and more

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.100
aggressive than their targets.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.409
They use physical attacks like
kicking, hitting, punching and shoving.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.200
Physical bullying is the easiest to
identify and most likely, what people

00:00:18.209 --> 00:00:22.040
think of when they think of bullying
as this receives more attention from

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:23.560
schools than other more subtle forms.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.860
Rhiannon: Verbal bullying uses
words, and name-calling to gain

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.760
power and control over a victim,

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.409
relentlessly insulting
and belittling them.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:37.090
This is often based on the way a child
or young person looks or acts and

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:41.210
is often directed towards those with
disabilities or special educational needs.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.380
Verbal bullying almost always occurs,
when adults aren’t around and when

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:50.270
victims do speak out, they are told to
‘ignore it’ but they should be listened

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:52.749
to, as it can leave deep emotional scars.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.980
Leah: Emotional bullying is
sneaky and insidious and often

00:00:56.980 --> 00:00:58.390
goes unnoticed by parents and

00:00:58.390 --> 00:00:58.960
teachers.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.569
It is often used by young
adolescents to ruin their target’s

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:06.089
social standing, by spreading
rumours, or breaking confidences.

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:09.230
This type of bullying is
most often used by girls.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.969
Rhiannon: Cyberbullying is
bullying via the Internet, using a

00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:14.850
smartphone, or other technology to

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.679
harass, threaten, embarrass,
or target another person.

00:01:21.599 --> 00:01:23.270
It often involves the posting of

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:26.780
hurtful images, online threats,
and sending offensive or

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.669
discriminatory emails or texts.

00:01:29.219 --> 00:01:33.620
Technology makes cyberbullies feel
anonymous and detached from the situation

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:37.740
whilst enabling them to target others
anytime, even in their own homes.

00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:41.600
Leah: Sexual Bullying can
involve, sexual name-calling,

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.759
crude comments, vulgar gestures,

00:01:43.880 --> 00:01:48.420
uninvited touching, sexual propositioning,
and use of pornographic materials.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.560
In extreme cases, it can
lead to sexual assault.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.060
Girls are most often the target
of this, but they can be targeted

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.890
both by boys and other girls.

00:01:57.719 --> 00:02:01.820
‘Sexting’ [texts with sexual content]
also can lead to sexual bullying.

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:06.490
If a girl sends a photo of herself to a
boyfriend, he may, in anger share that

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:10.800
photo publicly if they break up and
contrary to her wishes or intentions.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:15.540
Rhiannon: Prejudicial bullying, is
based on prejudices children and young

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.350
people may have towards different
races, religions, or sexual orientation.

00:02:20.929 --> 00:02:24.890
Often, this type of bullying is
severe and can lead to hate crimes.

00:02:25.519 --> 00:02:28.959
Any time a child is bullied for
their sexual orientation, race, or

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.690
religion, it should be reported.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.940
Leah: The motivation of bullies, are
all different and not all bullies

00:02:34.969 --> 00:02:36.830
will fit neatly into a category.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.929
Some bullies will fall into several
categories and some may appear to

00:02:40.949 --> 00:02:42.420
be in a category all their own.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.300
Rhiannon: Some individuals become
bullies because they were once bullied

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.390
themselves and this is very common.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:53.070
Others have big egos and a group of
followers and bully to keep their

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.720
Power or social standing.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:59.730
Some bully out of jealousy and others
seem pleasant on the outside, but are

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:01.560
cold and calculating on the inside.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:05.410
Leah: Bullies can also work
in groups or cliques, but when

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:06.709
they are on their own, behave

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:07.330
differently.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.530
Some bullies are just totally indifferent
to the feelings of others and can

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.440
have deep psychological problems.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:17.239
Rhiannon: Whatever the type of bully,
all bullying is wrong and should

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.880
not be tolerated, as it can have a
devastating effect on children and

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:22.510
young people's mental well-being.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:26.530
It is something we should always be
mindful of and on the lookout for.

